WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.784
Roman symbols include I equals 1, V equals 5, X equals 10, L equals 50 and C equals

00:00:07.784 --> 00:00:11.997
100. Use IV, IX, XL and XC for subtraction forms.

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:19.573
Write 40 as a Roman numeral. The answer is XL. Roman numerals use I, V, X, L and C:

00:00:19.573 --> 00:00:20.632
40 equals XL.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:26.869
A clock label at a farm is XLII. What number is it? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:34.935
A clock label at a farm is XLII. What number is it? The answer is 42. XLII represents

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:35.337
42.
